176 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 112 0 R
/T (With the rapid advancement in wireless communication and radar technologies, there is a growing demand for antenna systems that are compact, efficient, and capable of supporting multiple functionalities. One such critical application area is Synthetic Aperture Radar \(SAR\), which is widely used for high-resolution imaging in remote sensing, surveillance, and environmental monitoring.)
/E (With the rapid advancement in wireless communication and radar technologies, there is a growing demand for antenna systems that are compact, efficient, and capable of supporting multiple functionalities. One such critical application area is Synthetic Aperture Radar \(SAR\), which is widely used for high-resolution imaging in remote sensing, surveillance, and environmental monitoring.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
177 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 112 0 R
/T (In recent years, the integration of Multiple Input Multiple Output \(MIMO\) technology with SAR systems has significantly enhanced system performance. MIMO technology enables the use of multiple transmitting and receiving antennas, which improves spatial resolution, signal quality, and data reliability. However, implementing MIMO-SAR systems requires antennas that can operate efficiently with multiple channels while maintaining low mutual coupling and high isolation.)
/E (In recent years, the integration of Multiple Input Multiple Output \(MIMO\) technology with SAR systems has significantly enhanced system performance. MIMO technology enables the use of multiple transmitting and receiving antennas, which improves spatial resolution, signal quality, and data reliability. However, implementing MIMO-SAR systems requires antennas that can operate efficiently with multiple channels while maintaining low mutual coupling and high isolation.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
