555 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 128 0 R
/E (In this project, a compact dual-band dual-polarized microstrip antenna array has been successfully designed and implemented for MIMO-SAR applications. The antenna system was developed using microstrip technology and simulated using CST Microwave Studio.)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
556 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 128 0 R
/E (The proposed design effectively achieves dual-band operation, allowing the antenna to function at two different frequency ranges. This enhances the flexibility and usability of the antenna in advanced radar systems. Additionally, the incorporation of dual polarization improves signal diversity and reduces interference, which is essential for efficient MIMO performance.)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
557 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 128 0 R
/E (The use of an antenna array configuration significantly improves the gain and directivity of the system, making it suitable for applications such as SAR imaging and remote sensing. The implementation of a corporate feeding network ensures equal power distribution among all elements, leading to stable and reliable performance.)
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
